From 19ef7c7b2509d87057b7f136ae8ba59ff7c2c6fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:04:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Send the CW ID when the host asks for it with CWID ON

CWID ON and CWID OFF were answered OK and dropped, so the HF session's
cwid flag was only ever set in tests, and a station whose call is not of
the US kind never identified in CW. Pat sends CWID ON each time it
starts its varahf modem, and operators outside the US have to identify
their transmissions too.

CWID ON now sets the flag and CWID OFF clears it, in the station's
config and the running session's, as P2P SESSION does. Without either,
nothing changes: a US call identifies and other calls do not. A US call
still identifies after CWID OFF, as before. VARA FM still answers WRONG.

cwid_follows_the_host counts the keys of a call nobody answers, with
RETRIES 2: two connect requests, then the CW ID if there is one. It
fails on v0.1.3 for XX0A with CWID ON.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
